{"schema_version":"1.9.2","id":"RLSA-2026:103838","published":"2026-11-28T06:02:25.488520Z","modified":"2026-11-28T06:30:02.457224541Z","upstream":["CVE-2026-63916","CVE-2026-98741","CVE-2026-99236","CVE-2026-99362"],"summary":"Critical: kernel-rt security, bug fix, and enhancement update","details":"The kernel-rt packages provide the Real Time Linux Kernel, which enables fine-tuning for systems with extremely high determinism requirements.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: HID: wacom: Fix OOB write in wacom_hid_set_device_mode() (CVE-2026-63916)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: ua101: reject mismatched capture/playback packet sizes (CVE-2026-98741)\n\n* kernel: kernel: privilege escalation via incomplete event filter expressions (CVE-2026-99236)\n\n* kernel: kernel: Out-of-bounds write in nfsd via crafted SEQUENCE compound requests (CVE-2026-99362)\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* kswapd0 loops in do_shrink_slab holding shrinker_rwsem after list_lru_count_one returns a negative nr_items as unsigned long, system hangs (JIRA:Rocky Linux-300411)\n\n* [Rocky Linux 8] vlan-tagged GSO packets are dropped in __dev_queue_xmit with SKB_DROP_REASON_SKB_BAD_GSO (JIRA:Rocky Linux-307055)\n\n* Rocky Linux 8 error in device recovery while iscsi is in use (JIRA:Rocky Linux-307720)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.","affected":[{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-debug","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-debug?distro=rocky-linux-8&epoch=0"},"ranges":[{"type":"ECOSYSTEM","events":[{"introduced":"0"},{"fixed":"0:4.18.0-553.190.1.rt7.531.el8_10"}],"database_specific":{"yum_repository":"NFV"}}],"database_specific":{"source":"https://storage.googleapis.com/resf-osv-data/RLSA-2026:103838.json"}},{"package":{"name":"kernel-rt-modules","ecosystem":"Rocky Linux:8","purl":"pkg:rpm/rocky-linux/kernel-rt-modules?distro=